@bryan_johnson @ESYudkowsky I'm obviously not Eliezer, but I expect his answer to be very pessimistic, and I would agree with him.

Safely aligning AI under the current paradigm essentially requires solving mechanistic interpretability - at minimum!

Solving mech interp seems 𝘷𝘦𝘳𝘺 unlikely to happen.

@icpolicy @jon3k If we know how LLMs work, then what do you think the field of Mechanistic Interpretability exists for?

Does Anthropic hire mech interp researchers as some charade?

Are they just pretending they don't know how LLMs work, and then presenting their "findings" for the fun of it?
